 ALS\n\nThe CM32183 and CM36781 ALS drivers did not populate the calibration\ntemperature output parameter in their get_offset implementations, and\nhost_cmd_motion_sense() declared out_temp without an initializer. When\nthe AP issued MOTIONSENSE_CMD_SENSOR_OFFSET or\nMOTIONSENSE_CMD_PERFORM_CALIB for these sensors, uninitialized EC stack\nbytes were copied into the host command response buffer.\n\nSet *temp to EC_MOTION_SENSE_INVALID_CALIB_TEMP in cm32183_get_offset()\nand cm36781_get_offset() to match other ALS drivers, and default-initialize\nout_temp in host_cmd_motion_sense() as defense-in-depth across offset,\nscale, and calibration host commands.\n\nBUG\u003db:516277361\nTEST\u003dtwister -c -T zephyr/test/drivers -s drivers.host_cmd.ec_host_cmd\n```\n\nSuggested commit messages if split into two CLs:\n- **Driver CL**:\n```text\ndriver: als: Set invalid calibration temp in cm32183 and cm36781 get_offset\n\ncm32183_get_offset() and cm36781_get_offset() wrote the sensor offset\nbut left the calibration temperature output parameter (*temp)\nuninitialized. Populate *temp with EC_MOTION_SENSE_INVALID_CALIB_TEMP to\nfulfill the motion_sense get_offset driver contract and match other ALS\ndrivers.\n\nBUG\u003db:516277361\nTEST\u003dtwister -c -T zephyr/test/drivers -s drivers.default.ec_host_cmd\n```\n- **Host command CL**:\n```text\nmotion_sense: Initialize out_temp in host_cmd_motion_sense\n\nDefault-initialize out_temp to EC_MOTION_SENSE_INVALID_CALIB_TEMP in\nhost_cmd_motion_sense() so that MOTIONSENSE_CMD_SENSOR_OFFSET,\nMOTIONSENSE_CMD_SENSOR_SCALE, and MOTIONSENSE_CMD_PERFORM_CALIB cannot\nleak uninitialized stack bytes to the AP if a sensor driver fails to\npopulate *temp.\n\nBUG\u003db:516277361\nTEST\u003dtwister -c -T zephyr/test/drivers -s drivers.host_cmd.ec_host_cmd\n```\n\n[🔗](http://go/tj/87cbd56f-5d12-4e57-ba09-223ce48a56f9)",
