      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] **Driver Unit Test Coverage \u0026 Pre-existing `offset[Y]` / `offset[Z]` Initialization**\n\n1. **Unit test coverage**: Neither `cm32183_get_offset` nor `cm36781_get_offset` has a unit test verifying that `drv-\u003eget_offset()` sets `*temp \u003d EC_MOTION_SENSE_INVALID_CALIB_TEMP` (compare `test_tcs_get_set_offset` in `zephyr/test/drivers/default/src/tcs3400.c`). Adding a small driver test that pre-populates `int16_t temp \u003d 0;` and asserts `zassert_equal(EC_MOTION_SENSE_INVALID_CALIB_TEMP, temp);` after calling `drv-\u003eget_offset(s, offset, \u0026temp)` will guard against regressions in both drivers.\n\n2. **Suggestion for a follow-up CL (pre-existing code)**: `host_cmd_motion_sense()` passes `int16_t offset[3]` (`out-\u003esensor_offset.offset`) to `sensor-\u003edrv-\u003eget_offset()`. Other ALS drivers (`tcs3400_get_offset` in `driver/als_tcs3400.c` and `veml3328_get_offset` in `driver/als_veml3328.c`) explicitly zero `offset[Y]` and `offset[Z]`:\n```c\noffset[X] \u003d CM32183_GET_DATA(s)-\u003eoffset;\noffset[Y] \u003d 0;\noffset[Z] \u003d 0;\n```\nHere (and in `driver/als_cm36781.c`), `*offset \u003d ...` only writes `offset[0]`, leaving `offset[1]` and `offset[2]` uninitialized if a caller does not zero the output buffer beforehand.\n\nOther locations with the same pattern:\n- `driver/als_cm36781.c` **lines 95-101** (`cm36781_get_offset`)\n\n[🔗](http://go/tj/87cbd56f-5d12-4e57-ba09-223ce48a56f9)",
